1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,233
This is Video Studio.

2
00:00:02,233 --> 00:00:04,500
You ask Claude for a video in one sentence,

3
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:06,000
and you get back a finished,

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,967
narrated MP4.

5
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:12,700
Open the repo in Claude Code and say what you need.

6
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:14,933
A marketing video for a website.

7
00:00:14,933 --> 00:00:16,967
A tutorial for your app.

8
00:00:16,967 --> 00:00:19,033
Or an explainer from your docs.

9
00:00:20,467 --> 00:00:22,267
Claude starts with research.

10
00:00:22,267 --> 00:00:26,433
It visits the website, takes screenshots and reads the pages.

11
00:00:26,433 --> 00:00:29,567
For an app, it clicks through in a read-only browser,

12
00:00:29,567 --> 00:00:31,167
so nothing gets changed.

13
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:35,000
Next, it writes a short script,

14
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,100
and records a natural voice-over for each scene with ElevenLabs.

15
00:00:40,533 --> 00:00:42,500
The scenes are built in code,

16
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:44,100
with React and Three.

17
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:45,200
js.

18
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:47,900
Every animation is timed to the words,

19
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:50,400
so things appear right as they're said.

20
00:00:51,833 --> 00:00:54,000
You can review a storyboard first.

21
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,233
Then it renders the video with captions,

22
00:00:56,233 --> 00:00:58,700
and checks the file before it hands it over.

23
00:01:00,133 --> 00:01:01,900
Your videos stay private.

24
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:04,233
They live in folders that git ignores,

25
00:01:04,233 --> 00:01:06,967
so only the examples are in the public repo.

26
00:01:08,367 --> 00:01:10,533
To get started, clone the repo,

27
00:01:10,533 --> 00:01:13,133
install it, and add your ElevenLabs key.

28
00:01:13,133 --> 00:01:14,667
Then just ask.

29
00:01:14,667 --> 00:01:17,100
This video was made exactly that way.
